.TH SDL_FlushIO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_FlushIO \- Flush any buffered data in the stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_FlushIO(SDL_IOStream *context);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function makes sure that any buffered data is written to the stream\[char46] Normally this isn\(aqt necessary but if the stream is a pipe or socket it guarantees that any pending data is sent\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I context

.BR SDL_IOStream
structure to flush\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_OpenIO (3),
.BR SDL_WriteIO (3)
